// A2 course (A1 → A2 roadmap), module 4 „Kodu ja ümbrus” (a2-016…020), level A2. Lesson template v4
// (docs/COURSE_DESIGN_COMMUNICATIVE.md §12, docs/METHODOLOGY_STANDARD.md). One storyline, one year before the B1
// course (docs/COURSE_CAST.md): Sofia (27) rents a room from Malle Pärn (66) in Mustamäe, Akadeemia tee 30-12 (5th
// floor, no lift), flatmate Grete (22, student, works at weekends); house manager Arvo Lind, neighbour below Helju,
// härra Sepp (3rd floor, module 1). Goal, said on the first sheet: at the end the learner reads flat ads, calls about
// one and writes what kind of home they want (019 Kasuta, final project). Sofia only looks: she stays at Malle's
// until she has a job (the B1 course moves her to Kalamaja).
//   016 Sofia's room at Malle's — kus? -s (köögis, toas) and „Köögis on laud”; rooms and furniture; Viktor helps
//       with Malle's new sofa; video call with mother Helgi.
//   017 a small flood (the washing machine hose) — the short illative (lühike sisseütlev): koju, poodi, kooli, linna,
//       tuppa, kööki, sauna, pähe, kinno next to -sse (keldrisse, esikusse; majja = majasse); kus? / kuhu? / kust?;
//       calling the house manager. Grammar item of the module (A2 grammar plan: 04 short illative).
//   018 Viktor's farm in Kõrvemaa with the sauna — peal: -l / -le / -lt (laual, tööle, maale, turult), against sees;
//       the short illative again (sauna, järve, tuppa); a sauna evening for Jaan's family.
//   019 Mustamäe and a flat of her own — postpositions with the genitive (poe kõrval, pargi vastas, maja lähedal),
//       asuma; an estate agent (Raul Pihl), ads, the call and the message (final project); short illative again
//       (kesklinna, keelekooli, raamatukokku).
// Recycling of module 3 (päev, kell, harjumused): hommikul, õhtul, kell, pool, tavaliselt, sageli, mõnikord, iga päev,
// ärkama, puhkama, magama, kõigepealt, siis, pärast, nädalavahetus. Harno A2 formats trained: short-answer listening
// (played twice), dialogue T/F, set phrases MC, signs and ads matching, a letter with 3-option gaps, a ~150-word text,
// a message ≥ 30 words, picture description, question cards in pairs. Lesson 5 is the module's check (unchanged).
// The v3 file is in archive/v3/a2/module04.js.
